From: Chitkul Lakshya <chitkullakshya@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 16:01:05 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat: validate-first voice ack pipeline with cached TTS

Eliminates false acknowledgments and audio/animation desync by:
- Validating commands with local TS parser BEFORE saying "On it sir"
- Pre-synthesizing 5 ack phrases in Rust for instant (<5ms) playback
- Emitting tts:audio-started event to sync orb hide + loading show
- Connecting loading indicator to all backend query paths

Root causes fixed:
1. isLongRunningQuery() regex fired before validation, acking garbage STT
2. speak() took 200-1700ms to start audio, orb hid before sound
3. Invalid commands could get both "On it sir" + "Didn't catch that"
4. Loading indicator only showed for long-running queries, not all

RAM cost: +528 KB after first speak (0.09% of idle RAM)
New deps: 0

Generated with [Devin](https://devin.ai)

